instr:
`parseEquation()` throws `not implemented` when starting an algebra derivation

Trying to wire wyrm-math's algebra gestures into an interface, I hit an exception before I can offer a legal move or navigate its derivation history:

```ts
import { Derivation, parseEquation, enumerateMoves, ruleById } from "wyrm-math";
const d = new Derivation(parseEquation("4x + 7 = 23"));
const move = enumerateMoves(d.current).find(m => m.ruleId === "move-term-across")!;
d.apply(ruleById(move.ruleId), move.location, move.params);
d.undo();
d.redo();
```

This should parse the equation, offer an applicable move, and let undo/redo navigate the resulting history. Fill in the throwing stubs across parsing, exact arithmetic support, assumptions, branching derivations, move enumeration, captions, problem generation, and equation systems. The expected behaviour is described in the API doc comments and `FEATURE.md`.

The affected files are `src/parse.ts`, `src/derivation.ts`, `src/moves.ts`, `src/assumptions.ts`, `src/describe.ts`, `src/eval.ts`, `src/expr.ts`, `src/rational.ts`, `src/rule.ts`, `src/generate.ts`, and `src/system.ts`. Under `src/rules/`, the affected files are `addToBothSides.ts`, `combineFractions.ts`, `expandPower.ts`, `factorOut.ts`, `identities.ts`, `multiplicativeCancellation.ts`, `multiplyBothSides.ts`, `powers.ts`, `quadratics.ts`, `quotientOfPowers.ts`, `reduceIntegerFraction.ts`, `roots.ts`, and `splitTerm.ts`.

